    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithvi-narayan-shah">Prithvi Narayan Shah</a> of Gorkha, who conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a> in 1768–1769.</li><li>Defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1814–1816 fixed its borders; hereditary Rana prime ministers ruled in the king’s name from 1846 to 1951.</li><li>Popular movements and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepalese-civil-war">Maoist insurgency</a> ended the monarchy, which the Constituent Assembly abolished in 2008.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithvi-narayan-shah">Prithvi Narayan Shah</a> called his kingdom ‘a yam between two boulders’, squeezed between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a>, a phrase still quoted in debates on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>’s foreign policy.</p></aside>
    </section>

